      "boundElements": [], "updated": 1, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20, "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "Workspace Secrets DR - direct cross-workspace replication (diff & apply; no S3, no CRR, no KMS)",
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Workspace Secrets DR - direct cross-workspace replication (diff & apply; no S3, no CRR, no KMS)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25, "baseline": 20, "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle", "version": 2, "versionNonce": 102, "index": "a1", "id": "band",
      "x": 50, "y": 64, "width": 1640, "height": 70, "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44", "backgroundColor": "#ebfbee", "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": { "type": 3 }, "seed": 1002,
      "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": [], "updated": 1, "link": null, "locked": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "version": 2, "versionNonce": 103, "index": "a2", "id": "bandt",
      "x": 62, "y": 72, "width": 1616, "height": 58, "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1003, "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [], "updated": 1, "link": null, "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12, "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "Standalone DR for Databricks workspace secrets (scopes, values, ACLs). A single REPLICATE job runs in the ACTIVE workspace (us-east-2) as the DR service principal: it reads the SOURCE secrets, reads the DESTINATION (us-west-2) secrets cross-workspace via the Secrets API (no compute on the passive side), diffs by value hash + ACL signature, and pushes ONLY the delta into the destination. Values move over TLS; both secret stores are encrypted at rest by the platform. Direction is parameterized, so failover = replicate with the roles swapped (the secondary is a warm mirror). SDK-only -> runs in a notebook, a job, or locally.",
      "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Standalone DR for Databricks workspace secrets (scopes, values, ACLs). A single REPLICATE job runs in the ACTIVE workspace (us-east-2) as the DR service principal: it reads the SOURCE secrets, reads the DESTINATION (us-west-2) secrets cross-workspace via the Secrets API (no compute on the passive side), diffs by value hash + ACL signature, and pushes ONLY the delta into the destination. Values move over TLS; both secret stores are encrypted at rest by the platform. Direction is parameterized, so failover = replicate with the roles swapped (the secondary is a warm mirror). SDK-only -> runs in a notebook, a job, or locally.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25, "baseline": 12, "autoResize": false
    },

    { "type": "rectangle", "version": 2, "versionNonce": 110, "index": "b0", "id": "s0",
      "x": 50, "y": 164, "width": 630, "height": 104, "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2", "backgroundColor": "#e7f5ff", "fillStyle": "solid",
